    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "finding": "Finite identity safeguards are present; unbounded per-iteration IDs are not demonstrated",
      "strength": "code evidence, not a whole-domain termination proof",
      "details": "Family identity uses static scope/producer/bindings rather than the full input Data chain. Loop-summary-as-content is reduced to an opaque relation instead of nested embedding. Member identities use a static scope and family producer/selector; carried bindings use incoming/unresolved markers. The code therefore has real mechanisms against recursive ID growth. These do not imply small finite state space or prove every interacting path bounded.",
